---
/**
 * Where "Get an API key" and "Log in" go until the dashboard exists.
 *
 * There is no form because there is nothing behind a form: no account, no key issuing, no
 * session, and no endpoint on a static site to post to. A `mailto:` with the subject filled in
 * is the honest version of a waiting list, and the address is printed in full for the browsers
 * that do not open mail.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, CONTACT_MAILTO, CONTACT_SUBJECT } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Early access, Bookrail"
  description="Bookrail is not open for sign up yet. What exists today, and what has to exist before an API key does."
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Early access</h1>
    <p>
      There is no sign up yet, and no dashboard to log in to. Issuing an API key needs an account
      and a project you can see, and neither exists outside a developer machine today.
    </p>
    <p>What does exist, and what you can read right now:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The <a href="/docs/api/reference/">API reference</a>, generated from
        <a href="/openapi.json">the OpenAPI document</a> the server itself serves.
      </li>
      <li>
        The <a href="/docs/cli-basics/">CLI</a> and the
        <a href="/docs/mcp/">MCP server</a>, both installable with <code>npx</code> once they are
        published to npm.
      </li>
      <li>
        The <a href="/docs/concepts/">data model</a>, the
        <a href="/docs/guides/time-zones/">time zone rules</a> and the
        <a href="/docs/errors/">error catalogue</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Ask for early access</h2>
    <p>
      There is no form here, because there is nothing behind one. Write to
      <a href={CONTACT_MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, subject <code>{CONTACT_SUBJECT}</code>, and say
      what you are building and roughly how many bookings a month it makes. That is the whole
      process, and it is answered by a person.
    </p>
    <p>
      The address is <strong>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</strong>, in case your browser does not open mail
      for you. Nothing on this site collects anything: no form, no analytics, no cookies.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
